{{also|Martial}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|martialis|lang=la||of [[Mars]] (Roman god of war)}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/ˈmɑɹʃəl/|lang=en}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈmɑːʃəl/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-martial.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɑː(ɹ)ʃəl|lang=en}}
* {{homophones|lang=en|marshall}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of, relating to, or suggestive of war; [[warlike]].
#* Dryden
#*: But peaceful kings, o'er '''martial''' people set, / Each other's poise and counterbalance are.
# Relating to or connected with the [[armed forces]] or the profession of arms or military life.
# {{context|comparable|lang=en}} Characteristic of or befitting a [[warrior]]; having a military bearing; [[soldierly]], [[soldierlike]], [[warriorlike]].
# {{context|medicine|chemistry|obsolete|lang=en}} Relating to, or containing, [[iron]]; [[chalybeate]].
#: '''''martial''' preparations''
#: '''''martial''' flowers: a reddish crystalline salt of iron''

